---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | 50 Five-Star Hotels"
  description="Transparency about booking links, editorial independence and how 50 Five-Star Hotels handles commercial relationships."
>
  <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none
    prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-[#1F2428]
    prose-h1:text-4xl prose-h1:mb-8
    prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-10 prose-h2:mb-4
    prose-p:text-[#1F2428]/75 prose-p:leading-relaxed
    prose-strong:text-[#1F2428]">

    <p class="text-[#B88A44] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest not-prose mb-4">Transparency</p>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>

    <h2>Booking links</h2>
    <p>
      This website contains links to hotel booking platforms, including Booking.com. At the time of launch, these are standard search links, not affiliate links — clicking them and booking will not generate any commission for this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      If affiliate links are added in the future, this disclosure will be updated clearly. If you book through a future affiliate link, the site may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      Hotels are included in this site because they appear to offer unusually strong value, not because of commercial arrangements, commissions or payments. No hotel has paid to be featured here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Editorial judgement comes first. The scoring, verdicts and written profiles reflect an honest assessment of each hotel's value case, including its weaknesses and cautions.
    </p>

    <h2>Prices and accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Prices change constantly. All price references on this site are approximate and reflect rates that have been observed during research periods. They are not guarantees of current or future availability.
    </p>
    <p>
      Always check the final rate, taxes, room type, location and cancellation policy directly with the booking platform before making any travel decision. Hotel experiences can also vary by room category, season and management changes.
    </p>

    <h2>Five-star designations</h2>
    <p>
      Star ratings are derived from local classification systems, booking platform ratings or hotel self-designations. They are not universally standardised. Some hotels described as five-star here meet international luxury chain standards; others are local or booking-site five-star properties that are interesting for value reasons rather than star-rating equivalence. Each profile explains the relevant category clearly.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this disclosure or notice any inaccuracies, you are welcome to use the contact information on the <a href="/about" class="text-[#B88A44] hover:underline no-underline">about page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
